s of the Bakry–Émery curvature of connection graphs have been characterized in terms of the heat semigroup for functions and the heat semigroup for vector fields of the underlying graphs [35, Theorem 3.2]. In particular, we mention the following application of Bakry–Émery curvature of connection graphs to the spectral graph theory. Consider a finite graph $G=(V,E)$ with $|V|=N$, and a connection ${\\sigma }_{0}:{E}^{or}\\to O(1)=\\{\\pm 1\\}$ such that ${\\sigma }_{0}\\equiv -1$ . If the Bakry–Émery curvature of the connection graph $(G,{\\sigma }_{0})$ is lower bounded by K, then the maximal eigenvalue {\\lambda }_{N}${\\lambda }_{N}$ of the normalized graph Laplacian of G satisfies$2-{\\lambda }_{N}\\ge K.$ If, furthermore, K is nonnegative, we have that $2-{\\lambda }_{N}$ is of the same order as {\\beta }^{2}${\\beta }^{2}$ up to a constant depending only on the maximal degree, where β is the bipartiteness constant of Trevisan [48] or one minus the dual Cheeger constant of Bauer-Jost [7].\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStable solution of the log-Minkowski problem in the case of many hyperplane symmetries (https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.03395)\nciteturn1academia18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.8 years ago; In the case of symmetries with respect to n independent linear hyperplanes, the stability of the solution of the Logarithmic Minkowski problem on S^{n-1} is established.\nTitle: Stable solution of the log-Minkowski problem in the case of many hyperplane symmetries\nAuthors: Karoly J. Boroczky, Apratim De\nDate: Sat Jan  9 17:12:21 2021\n\nIn the case of symmetries with respect to n independent linear hyperplanes, the stability of the solution of the Logarithmic Minkowski problem on S^{n-1} is established.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStable Solution of the Logarithmic Minkowski Problem in the Case of Hyperplane Symmetries - Repository of the Academy's Library 